title: 'pallet-revive: fix callerIsRoot and callerIsOrigin across delegate calls'
doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    `System.callerIsRoot()` and `System.callerIsOrigin()` now find the caller of the contract
    asking the same way `msg.sender` does, so they return what `ISystem.sol` documents when the
    call path includes a delegate call. Behind a proxy, a Root dispatch now makes
    `callerIsRoot()` return `true` in the implementation, where it returned `false` before. A
    contract reached through a regular call made by delegated code now sees `false`, where it
    saw `true` before, so a contract that a Root dispatch reaches can no longer pass itself off
    as Root to another contract. `callerIsOrigin()` changes the same way for signed origins.
    Call paths without delegate calls are unchanged.

    Contracts behind a proxy that use `originIsRoot()` only because `callerIsRoot()` returned
    `false` there can switch to `callerIsRoot()` once the runtime includes this change.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    No configuration or migration is needed. The change applies to deployed contracts with the
    runtime upgrade that includes it.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
  validate: false
- name: pallet-revive-uapi
  bump: patch
